# Data Quality and Validation Standards

## Data Quality Checks
- MUST implement null checks on primary keys before processing
- MUST detect and handle duplicate records appropriately
- MUST validate referential integrity between related tables
- MUST implement volume checks with row count thresholds
- MUST validate data types and format consistency

## Validation Rules
- MUST define business rules for each data entity
- MUST implement range checks for numeric fields (e.g., prices, quantities)
- MUST validate date ranges and temporal consistency
- MUST check for data completeness across related entities
- MUST implement cross-table validation rules

## Error Handling
- MUST categorize data quality issues by severity (critical, warning, info)
- MUST implement graceful handling of data quality failures
- MUST provide detailed error messages with context
- MUST log data quality metrics for trend analysis
- MUST implement data quality dashboards for monitoring

## Data Profiling
- MUST generate data quality reports for each pipeline run
- MUST track data quality metrics over time
- MUST implement automated data profiling for new datasets
- MUST validate data distributions and patterns
- MUST monitor for data drift and anomalies

## Testing and Validation
- MUST include data quality tests in CI/CD pipeline
- MUST implement unit tests for validation logic
- MUST create test datasets with known data quality issues
- MUST validate data quality rules against business requirements
- MUST implement regression testing for data quality checks